Below is one possible decomposition of the mission description into a goal model for a multi‐robot system. In our design we break the mission into two main phases—a collection phase and a delivery phase—with built‐in battery management and an optional parallel mode for multiple storage locations. Each goal and task is annotated with its runtime structure (using sequential “;”, parallel “#”, or fallback “FALLBACK(… )” notation) and the type of decomposition (AND or OR) as required.

────────────────────────────
Step 1. Top-Level Goal  
────────────────────────────
G1: Complete Mission  
• Text: “Complete the mission of collecting required resources from storage locations and delivering them to the specified destination.”  
• Runtime: “;” (sequential)  
• Goal Type: Achieve  
• Target Condition: “All required resources are collected and delivered to the specified location.”  
• Relation: AND (with G2 and G3)  
• Justification: The mission must first collect resources then deliver them; both phases must be completed.

────────────────────────────
Step 2. Resource Collection Phase  
────────────────────────────
G2: Resource Collection Phase  
• Text: “Collect required resources from designated storage locations.”  
• Runtime: FALLBACK(G2.1, G2.2)  
  – Explanation: If the mission involves only one storage, the single‐storage procedure (G2.1) is used; if multiple storages are involved, then G2.2 (parallel collection) is applied.  
• Goal Type: Achieve  
• Target Condition: “All required resources are collected from storage.”  
• Relation: OR (between G2.1 and G2.2)  
• Justification: The collection phase may be performed either sequentially (for a single storage) or in parallel (for multiple storages) depending on the mission context.

────────────────────────────
Step 3a. Single Storage Collection  
────────────────────────────
G2.1: Collect from Single Storage  
• Text: “Collect a resource from a single storage location by navigating, requesting, and retrieving the resource.”  
• Runtime: “;” (sequential)  
• Goal Type: Achieve  
• Target Condition: “Resource is successfully collected from the designated single storage.”  
• Relation: AND (G2.1.1, G2.1.2, and battery management)  
• Justification: Each step in the collection process must be completed sequentially.

  ◦ G2.1.1: Navigate to Storage  
   – Text: “Navigate to the designated storage location based on path and waiting time estimation.”  
   – Runtime: “;” (sequential)  
   – Goal Type: Perform  
   – Relation: AND (followed by request)  
   – Justification: Navigation must be completed before the resource request.

  ◦ G2.1.2: Request and Retrieve Resource  
   – Text: “Send a precise message to the storage and wait for the resource retrieval.”  
   – Runtime: “;” (sequential)  
   – Goal Type: Perform  
   – Relation: AND (with navigation)  
   – Justification: The request and subsequent retrieval follow the navigation step.

  ◦ G2.1.3: Battery Management in Collection  
   – Text: “Monitor battery level during collection; if battery falls below 10%, return to the recharging station and reassign the mission.”  
   – Runtime: FALLBACK(AT5, AT6)  
   – Goal Type: Achieve  
   – Target Condition: “If battery low, mission is reassigned to another robot.”  
   – Relation: AND (integrated with the collection process)  
   – Justification: Ensures the robot can continue or safely reassign the task if its battery is too low.

────────────────────────────
Step 3b. Parallel Collection for Multiple Storages  
────────────────────────────
G2.2: Collect from Multiple Storages in Parallel  
• Text: “Collect resources from multiple storage locations concurrently using multiple robots.”  
• Runtime: “#” (parallel execution)  
• Goal Type: Achieve  
• Target Condition: “Resources from all designated storages are collected concurrently.”  
• Relation: AND (each storage’s collection must complete)  
• Justification: Parallel execution minimizes overall mission time when resources are spread across multiple storages.

────────────────────────────
Step 4. Resource Delivery Phase  
────────────────────────────
G3: Resource Delivery Phase  
• Text: “Deliver the collected resources to the specified destination, making multiple runs if necessary.”  
• Runtime: “;” (sequential)  
• Goal Type: Achieve  
• Target Condition: “All collected resources are delivered to the destination.”  
• Relation: AND (with G3.1 and G3.2)  
• Justification: Delivery is performed after collection and involves a series of sequential steps.

  ◦ G3.1: Deliver Resource  
   – Text: “Navigate to the destination and deliver the collected resources, repeating runs until all resources are delivered.”  
   – Runtime: “;” (sequential)  
   – Goal Type: Perform  
   – Relation: AND (with battery management)  
   – Justification: Delivery requires navigation and may need repeated runs to complete the delivery.

  ◦ G3.2: Battery Management in Delivery  
   – Text: “Monitor battery level during delivery; if battery falls below 30%, return the resource to a checkpoint and reassign the remaining task, or trigger an alert if the checkpoint return fails.”  
   – Runtime: FALLBACK(AT14, AT15)  
   – Goal Type: Achieve  
   – Target Condition: “If battery low, either return to checkpoint and reassign or trigger an alert if checkpoint return fails.”  
   – Relation: AND (integrated with the delivery process)  
   – Justification: Ensures safe delivery or proper alerting in low battery conditions.

